Dzień dobry Panie Mirosławie, hello Ewelina,

so, we are there. Attached is the clean addendum (KCC/FB/2024/S1, the PDF has Sofia's tracked changes accepted, the Word file still has them, ignore the Word file please). To make sure we are all reading the same thing before Wednesday, this is what it says, in my own words and in the order you will meet it:

- season runs 7 October 2024 to 31 March 2025 (you asked for 28 February, we gave you the extra month because the Valencia navel tail always runs late);
- lane is Rotterdam-Maasvlakte (RTM-3) to Gdynia (GDY-1) on our feeder, same boxes, same KC-Tag 4 loggers;
- discount is prospective and by band of boxes actually moved in the season: boxes 1 to 249 get 2 %, boxes 250 to 449 get 5.5 %, boxes 450 and up get 8.5 %;
- the 8.5 % band only exists because Fruttoria commits to at least 450 boxes, and if the season ends under 450 we invoice the difference between the 8.5 % and whatever band you actually reached on the boxes 250 and up (Sofia calls it a "true-up", I call it fair);
- payment 45 days from invoice date (not from delivery, Miroslaw asked and the answer is yes);
- 4 days free detention at the GDY-1 yard instead of the usual 3;
- fuel surcharge capped at 5.5 % of the leg fee;
- the Tidewalk monitoring fee is waived on the first 60 boxes.

Signing: Wednesday 2 October, 10:00, at your Pruszcz Gdański office, Pan Józef Marchwicki signs for Fruttoria and Dieter Ahlbeck-Roe for us. Rafał and I will be there, parking is a nightmare so we come by one car. Please send me the names for the visitor badges by Tuesday noon.

Best regards / pozdrawiam,
Yusuf

