Numbers, since Rafał sent me the new bands on Friday. Our floor for a lane is 21 % blended gross margin. At the old 3/6/9 bands and Fruttoria's forecast of 575 boxes the blended discount comes out at 4.8 % and the lane margin at 21.3 %, fine. At the new 2/5.5/8.5 bands with the lower thresholds the blended discount is 4.6 % and the lane blends to 21.4 %, so the lane as a whole is fine too. The problem is the 126 boxes that would sit in the top band: on their own they run at a 20.4 % margin, under the floor, and for any price exception we test every band separately. That is why this needs Dieter, not me. I can live with it for one season given the volume, but only with the 450 commitment, otherwise we are selling the top band to someone who may not deliver the boxes.

Payment terms: 45 days costs us about 0.3 % per 15 extra days at our cost of capital (7.2 % a year), so 45 vs our standard 30 is nothing; 60 days I would only have considered if the top band had stayed at 6 %.

Free detention day 4: ops (Jarek) says the GDY-1 yard can absorb it, until the end of March, not longer. Fine.

Priya

